	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Vikunja Alfred Workflow

Manage, search, reschedule, and create Vikunja tasks directly from Alfred with instant response times and automatic caching.

*Disclaimer: This workflow is vibecoded with AI assistance.*

---

## ⚡ Setup

1. **Create an API Token**:
   - In Vikunja, navigate to **Settings &gt; API Tokens**.
   - Create a token with read/write permissions for **Tasks**, **Projects**, and **User Settings**.

2. **Configure Workflow**:
   - In **Alfred Preferences &gt; Workflows &gt; Vikunja**, click **Configure Workflow** (or the `[x]` icon) and set:
     - `VIKUNJA_URL`: Your Vikunja instance URL (e.g. `cal.example.com` or `https://vikunja.example.com`).
     - `VIKUNJA_API_TOKEN`: The API token generated above.
     - `VIKUNJA_RANGE`: Default due date view (`today`, `week`, `7d`, `8d`, `2w`, `3m`, `1y`, or `all`; default: `today`).
     - `VIKUNJA_DEFAULT_PROJECT`: *(Optional)* Project title or ID for `vadd`. If blank, uses your Vikunja account's default project.
     - `VIKUNJA_CACHE_TTL`: Cache duration in seconds (default: `60`).

---

## 🚀 Commands &amp; Shortcuts

- **Hotkey**: Press `⌃R` (Control+R) anywhere in macOS to trigger Vikunja Tasks.

### `v` — View, Search &amp; Quick-Create Tasks
- **Browse Your Agenda**:
  - `v` — Open tasks due in configured range (plus overdue).
  - `v today` — Tasks due today (plus overdue).
  - `v week` — Tasks due this week (through Sunday).
  - `v 8d` / `v 14d` — Tasks due in the next 8 or 14 days.
  - `v 2w` / `v 3w` — Tasks due in the next 2 or 3 weeks.
  - `v 3m` / `v 6m` — Tasks due in the next 3 or 6 months.
  - `v 1y` — Tasks due in the next year.
- **Search within Range or Across All**:
  - `v &lt;search&gt;` — Searches across **all open tasks** across all projects (e.g. `v dishwasher`, `v taxes`).
  - `v 2w &lt;search&gt;` — Search restricted to tasks due in the next 2 weeks.
  - `v today &lt;search&gt;` — Search restricted to tasks due today.
- **Fallback Quick-Create**:
  - If no tasks match your search query, press `↩` (Enter) on the fallback item to instantly create the task in your default project!
- **Actions on any Task**:
  - `↩` (Enter): Open task in browser.
  - `⌘↩` (Cmd+Enter): Mark task as complete.
  - `⌥↩` (Option+Enter): Reschedule task (pick or type a new due date).
  - `⌘C`: Copy full task details (dates, repetition, priority, labels, URL, etc.).
  - `⌘L`: View full task details in Large Type.

### `vadd &lt;title&gt;` — Quick Add Task
Creates a new task with the given title in your default project.

### `vdue` — Reschedule Tasks (Standalone)
Searches across all open tasks to pick one and assign a new due date (you can also press `⌥↩` on any task in `v` or `vfilter`).
- Select a quick option (`In 1 hour`, `In 3 hours`, `Tonight`, `Tomorrow`, `This weekend`, `Next week`, `Clear due date`) or type freeform dates/times:
  - Relative time: `in 9 hours`, `9h`, `in 30 mins`, `in 2h 30m`, `+9h`
  - Specific time today: `5pm`, `17:30`, `noon`, `tonight`
  - Day with time: `tomorrow 9am`, `tomorrow 15:30`, `friday 2pm`
  - Relative date: `+3d`, `tomorrow`, `friday`, `weekend`
  - Explicit date/time: `2026-09-01 15:30`, `2026-09-01`, `09/01`
  - Clear date: `none`, `clear`, `no date`

### `vfilter` — Browse Projects &amp; Filters
Browse tasks scoped by specific Projects or Saved Filters.
- Selecting a project or filter lists its active tasks.
- `↩` opens in browser; `⌘↩` marks as complete; `⌥↩` reschedules.

### `vproject` — Set Default Project
Lists active projects. Selecting one sets it as your Vikunja account's default project for `vadd`.

---

## 🛠 Requirements
- macOS with `python3` available on `PATH`.
- Zero third-party Python dependencies.</string>
